# Implements port slice 2 (A2; q37): `add` takes two inputs, the header written in place for `op` one
# -- `apply(add 10)` is refused at the call, "incompatible entry signature" (the needle pins the
# call's place: before A2 the same phrase was said at the header, for the formal itself).
fn: add (int: a; int: b) int
    return: a + b
end: add

fn: apply (op(fn: (int: x) int) int(value)) int
    return: op(value)
end: apply

int: ok 7
if: apply(add 10) != 11
    ok: 1
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
